# MapLibre container sizing

MapLibre GL sets `position: relative` on the map container and **overrides** Tailwind `absolute` / `inset-*`.

## Symptom

Fullscreen (or parent) map shows an all-black / empty screen: canvas exists, style.json loads, but **no vector tiles** and `.maplibregl-map` has `clientHeight === 0`.

## Required pattern

Parent must have a definite size (e.g. `fixed inset-0`). Map container must use **percentage size**, not absolute inset:

```tsx
<div className="fixed inset-0">
  <div ref={mapContainerRef} className="h-full w-full" />
</div>
```

## Do not

- Put `absolute inset-0` on the MapLibre container (MapLibre replaces `position` → height collapses to 0).
- Assume the map painted correctly just because attribution or zoom controls appear — verify `clientHeight > 0` and tile requests.

## Also

- Call `map.resize()` after `load` / when the fullscreen shell paints.
- Serve workers from `/public/maplibre/` via `setWorkerUrl` (see `scripts/copy-maplibre-assets.mjs`); do not rely on the page URL as the worker script.
